     ccttll..ccoonnff — CAM Target Layer / iSCSI target daemon configuration file

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccttll..ccoonnff configuration file is used by the ctld(8) daemon.  Lines
     starting with ‘#’ are interpreted as comments.  The general syntax of the
     ccttll..ccoonnff file is:

           pidfile _p_a_t_h

           auth-group _n_a_m_e {
                 chap _u_s_e_r _s_e_c_r_e_t
                 ...
           }

           portal-group _n_a_m_e {
                 listen _a_d_d_r_e_s_s
                 discovery-auth-group _n_a_m_e
                 ...
           }

           target _n_a_m_e _{
                 auth-group _n_a_m_e
                 portal-group _n_a_m_e
                 lun _n_u_m_b_e_r {
                      path _p_a_t_h
                 }
                 ...
           }

